    "description": "## Summary\n\nDeal names and External Deal IDs need a source shortcode (Aug 25 sync decision), and two flows need the same Source→code mapping — without a single source of truth the CASE logic gets duplicated and drifts. **Solution: one formula field on Deal that translates the Source picklist into its shortcode, referenced by both naming flows (BUILD-247, BUILD-248).**\n\n## Current state\n\nDeal\\__c.Source_\\_c exists (picklist: Shurzy, Vectiq, WagerTech, PredictiveX; optional; blank on all existing Deals). No shortcode field or mapping exists anywhere in the org. Formula chosen over CMDT deliberately: 4 rarely-changing values, keeps both naming flows formula-only (no added DML/SOQL); revisit CMDT only if the source list grows.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. Create Deal\\__c.Source_Codec — Formula (Text): {{CASE(TEXT(Source_\\_c), \"Shurzy\",\"S\", \"Vectiq\",\"V\", \"WagerTech\",\"WT\", \"PredictiveX\",\"P\", \"\")}}\n2. Automation-only field: not on page layouts, available to reports.\n3. Field description must state that Source_Code__c — the price of skipping CMDT.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Each of the 4 picklist values returns its mapped code (S, V, WT, P).\n2. Blank Source__c returns \"\" (empty string), not an error.\n3. A new picklist value not yet in the CASE returns \"\" (known limitation, covered by the field description).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n* Flow changes (BUILD-247, BUILD-248).\n* CMDT-based mapping.\n\n",
